1
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:02,560
THIS SERIES IS A FICTIONAL WORK
PRODUCED SOLELY FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:03,920
THE CHARACTERS AND EVENTS DEPICTED
ARE ENTIRELY FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,040
WE DO NOT INTEND TO PROMOTE DISCRIMINATION
AGAINST ANY PROFESSION, GENDER, OR GROUP

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:05,920
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED
IN THE MAKING OF THIS SERIES

5
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,720
I'm not an artist anymore.

6
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,120
<i>I can't sing at the club either.</i>

7
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,640
<i>I think I should leave.</i>

8
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:11,920
<i>What did I do wrong?</i>

9
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:12,920
<i>I just told the truth.</i>

10
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,320
<i>Phatee really did stab someone.</i>

11
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:16,960
<i>I was tricked back then.</i>

12
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:19,520
<i>He raped me in the car.</i>

13
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:22,080
<i>Phatee was the one who covered it up.</i>

14
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,120
<i>He took the blame to protect me.</i>

15
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,160
I once promised someone

16
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:28,560
<i>that we'd sing onstage</i>

17
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:30,080
<i>and play guitar together.</i>

18
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,880
Phatee! Ranne!

19
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:34,200
Phatee! Ranne!

20
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,400
What? Is that all you've got?

21
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:41,560
You keep your head down while punching.

22
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:43,760
You're leaving your back wide open!

23
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:47,920
Hey!

24
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:50,640
If you're this pathetic, cancel the fight.

25
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:56,360
You're the one who should watch your back.

26
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:58,880
Is that so?

27
00:01:00,120 --> 00:01:02,200
That ten million is going to be mine.

28
00:01:06,360 --> 00:01:07,600
Don't let your guard down.

29
00:01:17,960 --> 00:01:19,800
Wanna take a shower together?

30
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,320
I'm not your playmate.

31
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,440
Or do you want to be more than friends?

32
00:02:32,880 --> 00:02:38,720
<i>Can I whisper it softly to your ear?</i>

33
00:02:44,880 --> 00:02:48,280
<i>Can I whisper it softly?</i>

34
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:11,200
<i>Can I whisper it softly to your ear</i>
<i>That I love you?</i>

35
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,040
Hey.

36
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:19,760
When will you stop singing
with your back turned?

37
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:22,520
If I'm going to face someone
while singing,

38
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:24,680
it has to be you.

39
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:31,120
You've started cracking jokes lately.

40
00:03:31,760 --> 00:03:33,200
I'm not joking.

41
00:03:33,280 --> 00:03:34,720
It's the truth.

42
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:37,480
Here's your drink.

43
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,360
You're back again?

44
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,720
Japan is just around the corner.

45
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,960
I'll have a mimosa.

46
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,200
You don't get employee perks anymore.

47
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,720
Full price for you, customer.

48
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:11,040
Wow, you're so stingy with me.

49
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,800
So are you back because you're broke?

50
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,160
Or were you expelled?

51
00:04:17,680 --> 00:04:18,839
No.

52
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:21,920
Linda said Tangmo and Yoyeh
would be gone for a week,

53
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,480
so she asked me to help out.

54
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:25,000
They're short-staffed.

55
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:28,280
Oh, right. I requested leave
from the university,

56
00:04:29,280 --> 00:04:30,720
saying I had to attend
a relative's funeral.

57
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:33,800
So I put your name down.
You don't mind, right?

58
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:35,680
Your relative died,

59
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:37,000
but you used my name?

60
00:04:37,080 --> 00:04:39,200
You little bastard!

61
00:04:39,280 --> 00:04:40,640
You're gonna get it!

62
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,480
Hey, Vann!

63
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,640
How come you're here?

64
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:54,920
I'm filling in for you.

65
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,160
Thanks a lot.

66
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:00,800
- Hey.
- Leaving already?

67
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,160
Make sure you bring back that million.

68
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:07,760
Hey.

69
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:08,920
So, how about we

70
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,200
make a guess for fun?

71
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,320
Between Tangmo,

72
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:13,480
Yoyeh,

73
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:15,400
and the others…

74
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:17,280
In this match, who's going to win?

75
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,400
Wanna bet? I'll write it all down.

76
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,720
Who's betting on whom?

77
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,840
Okay.

78
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:24,360
Then I'm betting on Tangmo.

79
00:05:24,440 --> 00:05:26,440
Good choice, Mr. Singer.

80
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:28,840
Because I'm going to win anyway.

81
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:31,360
What about you, Phatee?
Who are you picking?

82
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:34,400
Do I have to pay if I guess wrong?

83
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:36,280
I don't have any cash.

84
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:39,480
Who carries cash these days?

85
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:42,000
You can just scan and pay
with an e-wallet.

86
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:43,880
I threw my phone away.

87
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:44,960
Hey.

88
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:47,880
Want me to draw some cards and spoil it?

89
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:49,960
Whether Tangmo and Yoyeh will win?

90
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:55,560
Shit!

91
00:05:58,320 --> 00:05:59,640
A combo of bad omens.

92
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,560
One card was bad enough.

93
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:05,080
But three in a row? Wow.

94
00:06:05,160 --> 00:06:06,560
Enough, enough.

95
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:08,160
Tangmo is above fate anyway.

96
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:10,000
These cards can't touch him.

97
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,040
Talay's right.

98
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,680
I'll be waiting for good news!

99
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,160
Okay, thanks a lot, everyone.

100
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:19,840
I'm off. See you, everyone!

101
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:22,520
- Good luck!
- Good luck!

102
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,280
Don't come back covered in blood, Bro.

103
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,760
Okay, I've written everyone's bets down.

104
00:06:27,840 --> 00:06:29,920
081…

105
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,680
63442

106
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:36,000
As for you, Vann,

107
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:39,600
finish your drink
and go help wash the dishes.

108
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,400
The apron is behind the counter.

109
00:06:41,480 --> 00:06:43,760
What? I haven't even unpacked yet,

110
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,920
and you're already putting me to work.

111
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,680
I'll pay staff price for this drink, then.

112
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:50,160
You haven't started working.
Doesn't count.

113
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,360
Look.

114
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,640
Why are you raising your hand?

115
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:56,600
- 500?
- 500.

116
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,000
I ordered it for you.

117
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,440
Are you sure this is the place?

118
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:06,120
There's nothing here.

119
00:07:06,200 --> 00:07:08,720
Yeah, this is the location.

120
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,200
They said 10 p.m.

121
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,400
It's exactly 10 p.m.

122
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,400
Good night.

123
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,799
Hey, Mr. Writer.

124
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,920
How many lines have you written today?

125
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,840
Don't count lines.
Count characters instead.

126
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,800
Then,

127
00:08:53,880 --> 00:08:55,520
shall we find inspiration somewhere else?

128
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,440
This place has great customer service.

129
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,320
I think Talay fell for him first.

130
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,160
I think it was Sun.

131
00:09:12,680 --> 00:09:14,080
Ta-da!

132
00:09:14,160 --> 00:09:18,160
And this is the jar
where everyone can try their luck

133
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,840
and guess who fell for whom first

134
00:09:20,920 --> 00:09:22,960
between Sun and Talay.

135
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,040
Wanna place a bet?

136
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:29,040
I'm betting on Talay.

137
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:31,480
Wow.

138
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:33,760
You went all the way abroad to study,

139
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,640
and you're betting just 20 baht?

140
00:09:36,720 --> 00:09:37,840
How could you?

141
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,480
I exchanged all my cash for yen.

142
00:09:41,720 --> 00:09:43,040
I'll put some in for you.

143
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:46,320
Bet as much as you want.

144
00:09:50,240 --> 00:09:51,400
So rich!

145
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:52,960
I'm jealous.

146
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:56,040
But if you like investing,

147
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:58,080
there's another investment opportunity.

148
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:00,320
Ta-da!

149
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:03,240
Anyone want to ship these two?

150
00:10:03,320 --> 00:10:05,000
Talay and Mimi.

151
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:06,520
The OG couple.

152
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:07,760
Who's betting?

153
00:10:09,720 --> 00:10:10,600
Why?

154
00:10:11,320 --> 00:10:13,200
See? I've got no hope.

155
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:15,720
He's dating someone else today,
but maybe he'll date me tomorrow.

156
00:10:15,800 --> 00:10:17,320
- Wanna bet?
- I'm in.

157
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:20,720
- Go ahead.
- I've got exactly 300.

158
00:10:20,800 --> 00:10:22,920
I'll put 100 in each box.

159
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,480
One of them has to be right!

160
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:27,400
Good luck! Get rich!

161
00:10:27,480 --> 00:10:29,360
That's more than my salary!

162
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,400
Wanna bet?

163
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,880
What's this "get rich" talk I just heard?

164
00:10:40,960 --> 00:10:43,720
Don't tell me you're gambling in my club.

165
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,760
No!

166
00:10:44,840 --> 00:10:46,160
It's not gambling.

167
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:47,480
It's just…

168
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:49,600
a little guessing game.

169
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:51,520
We're just

170
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:54,000
guessing who fell for whom first

171
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:56,120
between Talay and Sun.

172
00:10:57,280 --> 00:10:58,520
Wanna bet?

173
00:10:58,600 --> 00:11:00,160
How about this?

174
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:02,520
Whoever gets lucky and wins

175
00:11:02,600 --> 00:11:05,640
must also put some money
into the club. Simple, right?

176
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,440
So you win either way.

177
00:11:08,680 --> 00:11:10,960
You work here, so you should
share the money with the club.

178
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,400
You're the only one left.

179
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,480
The two of them

180
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,560
are a test for each other, huh?

181
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:05,720
Come on in. Long time no see!

182
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:07,360
I'll get you some drinks. Come on!

183
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:08,760
Sit down, sit down!

184
00:12:10,440 --> 00:12:13,200
LAY LAMOE BEACH BAR

185
00:12:15,640 --> 00:12:16,880
Here you go.

186
00:12:23,560 --> 00:12:25,000
Whenever I can't think of anything,

187
00:12:25,520 --> 00:12:26,800
I like coming here to sit.

188
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:45,600
<i>Talay.</i>

189
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,560
<i>You finally answered.</i>

190
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:50,440
<i>I thought you were an introvert.</i>

191
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:52,880
<i>You didn't answer when I called before.</i>

192
00:12:52,960 --> 00:12:54,440
<i>You didn't read my messages either.</i>

193
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:57,840
I was busy back then.

194
00:12:58,640 --> 00:12:59,800
<i>So where are you now?</i>

195
00:13:00,360 --> 00:13:02,480
<i>So you're not busy with work anymore?</i>

196
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,640
<i>Are you free on Saturday?</i>

197
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:06,320
<i>Let's grab something to eat.</i>

198
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,800
<i>The cat in my room misses you so much.</i>

199
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:13,000
I'm busy. I have a date.

200
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:15,600
<i>Suit yourself, then.</i>

201
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,160
Why did you lie to her?

202
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,680
You're free on Saturday, aren't you?

203
00:13:24,800 --> 00:13:26,880
I don't like that she wants
something serious with me.

204
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:29,280
Why not try talking to her first?

205
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,920
She seems to really like you.

206
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:32,760
Why are you so closed off?

207
00:13:33,760 --> 00:13:35,320
If I don't feel anything,

208
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:36,960
I don't have to force myself, do I?

209
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,840
Besides, I didn't lie to her.

210
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:42,120
I really do have a date.

211
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:44,960
With you.

212
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,400
You're kidding.

213
00:13:52,680 --> 00:13:55,080
What? What are you thinking?

214
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:58,400
We're doing research right now,

215
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:00,360
simulating a date, aren't we?

216
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,600
So?

217
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:09,480
Let's hear what a protagonist
like you would suggest.

218
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:12,040
In a place like this,

219
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,320
where it's this romantic,

220
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:17,480
what would the characters do next?

221
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:22,040
Find somewhere quiet,

222
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:24,880
somewhere people won't see them.

223
00:14:26,160 --> 00:14:27,480
And then…

224
00:14:28,760 --> 00:14:31,400
What's going on in your head?

225
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:37,360
What? Maybe they'd
want to be alone together,

226
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:39,080
open up or do whatever they want.

227
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,160
What are you thinking now?

228
00:14:41,680 --> 00:14:44,480
It's a romance novel, not an NSFW novel.

229
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:48,680
And then?

230
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:57,920
It depends.

231
00:14:58,440 --> 00:15:00,360
They could take it back to the room,

232
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:02,840
or do it right here.

233
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:20,280
Sorry.

234
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:24,040
What? Some kid chasing you?

235
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:30,160
<i>There's news about Pee again.</i>

236
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:33,440
<i>Pee's released a new book.</i>
<i>It's all over the damn news.</i>

237
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:05,080
Cha! What the fuck are you doing here?

238
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:06,560
None of your business.

239
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:15,840
Yoyeh.

240
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:24,160
Ahem.

241
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:30,880
Now that you're all here,

242
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:35,840
allow me to explain the rules
of this Werewolf game.

243
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:41,200
This is a reality game

244
00:16:42,920 --> 00:16:44,120
with surveillance cameras

245
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:46,800
recording throughout this mansion 24/7.

246
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,080
All of you must live here

247
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,840
and play the game here for seven days.

248
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:56,720
The villagers must survive
the wolves' hunt.

249
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,760
Whoever is the last one standing

250
00:17:00,640 --> 00:17:03,960
will take home a prize of
ten million baht.

251
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:07,800
Among the ten players,

252
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:11,200
there are two wolves in disguise,

253
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:12,480
one bodyguard,

254
00:17:13,880 --> 00:17:15,680
and seven villagers.

255
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:20,000
You'll find out your role

256
00:17:20,839 --> 00:17:22,000
inside this envelope.

257
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,760
Be careful.

258
00:17:29,440 --> 00:17:31,400
Don't let anyone find out

259
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,200
what role you've been assigned.

260
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:36,800
Otherwise,

261
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:40,360
you may be eliminated sooner
than you think.

262
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:49,520
Each day,

263
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:51,840
there will be a mini-game.

264
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:54,200
The winner will receive a prize

265
00:17:54,280 --> 00:17:56,520
or a clue as to who the wolves are.

266
00:17:58,280 --> 00:18:00,520
And every evening at 6 p.m.,

267
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:01,880
everyone must gather

268
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:03,880
in the Moon Room

269
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:07,840
to vote on who the hidden wolves are.

270
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,400
And if a player

271
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,720
correctly identifies a wolf,

272
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,360
the wolf will be burned

273
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:20,040
and eliminated from the game.

274
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:22,120
But if

275
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:24,960
the players fail to identify a wolf,

276
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,280
that night,

277
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:29,120
the wolves will hunt

278
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:30,640
and devour the villagers.

279
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:35,160
Please proceed.

280
00:20:36,280 --> 00:20:39,040
<i>Everyone, please place your devices,</i>
<i>including smartphones</i>

281
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:40,880
<i>in the bags held by our rabbits.</i>

282
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:43,320
<i>They'll keep them until the game ends.</i>

283
00:20:46,800 --> 00:20:49,440
<i>Everyone, please place your devices,</i>
<i>including smartphones,</i>

284
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:51,160
<i>in the bags held by our rabbits.</i>

285
00:20:51,240 --> 00:20:53,920
<i>They'll keep them until the game ends.</i>

286
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:01,440
The game will end on the seventh night.

287
00:21:01,520 --> 00:21:04,920
Whether you're a wolf, a villager,

288
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,040
or a bodyguard,

289
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:09,240
there will be only one winner,

290
00:21:10,280 --> 00:21:12,840
who will take home ten million baht.

291
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:18,000
What if the villagers vote out all
the wolves before the game ends?

292
00:21:19,640 --> 00:21:23,360
Would the remaining villagers have to
split the prize money?

293
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:29,040
In that case, we'll have a special game

294
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,600
to narrow down the villagers

295
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,840
to just one ultimate winner.

296
00:21:36,080 --> 00:21:36,960
Ready?

297
00:21:41,080 --> 00:21:42,840
Now, if everyone's ready,

298
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:47,840
let the game of Werewolf begin now.

299
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:48,800
Please proceed.

300
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,960
<i>Player May, out.</i>

301
00:22:28,800 --> 00:22:31,200
<i>Player Natty, out.</i>

302
00:23:20,800 --> 00:23:24,240
- Fuck! Why'd you shoot me?
- <i>Player Nack, out.</i>

303
00:23:28,880 --> 00:23:30,840
Sorry, the barrel was pointing left.

304
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:34,360
- <i>Player Ploen, out.</i>
- Damn it!

305
00:23:44,640 --> 00:23:45,920
You little bastard!

306
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:55,280
Why is he so good at escaping?

307
00:23:55,360 --> 00:23:56,640
Hey! Hey!

308
00:23:58,400 --> 00:23:59,760
You're not getting away!

309
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:01,760
Stop!

310
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:08,800
Hey! Who the fuck was that?

311
00:24:23,640 --> 00:24:25,560
<i>Player Wut, out.</i>

312
00:24:31,080 --> 00:24:32,160
Are you okay?

313
00:24:39,480 --> 00:24:40,800
Get down!

314
00:24:41,680 --> 00:24:43,120
Go! Go!

315
00:25:08,840 --> 00:25:11,000
Hey, four-eyes!

316
00:25:12,600 --> 00:25:14,320
Where the hell are you?

317
00:25:14,400 --> 00:25:15,920
Four-eyes!

318
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:21,480
<i>Player Au, out.</i>

319
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:34,440
I just slipped up.

320
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:54,760
Hey, there's a door over there!

321
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:56,400
Go!

322
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:07,600
- Tangmo.
- My gun isn't working.

323
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:16,320
You almost took a critical hit.

324
00:26:19,960 --> 00:26:22,400
Your skills have really declined
since you went solo.

325
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:25,640
I think I should be the one saying that.

326
00:26:26,400 --> 00:26:28,880
Don't forget, I'm the one
pointing a gun at you.

327
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:31,280
Go ahead and shoot if you dare.

328
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:39,760
Typical of you. Never plan ahead.

329
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:48,600
Yoyeh!

330
00:26:58,280 --> 00:26:59,080
Fuck!

331
00:27:05,480 --> 00:27:07,880
<i>Player Yoyeh, out.</i>

332
00:27:08,880 --> 00:27:10,880
<i>Player Cha, out.</i>

333
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:13,720
<i>Player Tangmo, out.</i>

334
00:27:19,200 --> 00:27:20,840
<i>The game is over.</i>

335
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:23,000
<i>The winner is Player Ohm.</i>

336
00:27:23,080 --> 00:27:26,160
<i>Please choose between a cash prize</i>
<i>or a clue.</i>

337
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:28,600
I'll take the money.

338
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:30,000
I'll take the money!

339
00:27:30,840 --> 00:27:32,880
You guys just walked
right into my line of fire.

340
00:27:32,960 --> 00:27:34,840
Just wait and see.

341
00:27:34,920 --> 00:27:36,240
This four-eyes right here

342
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:37,760
will beat you all!

343
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:44,480
<i>The winner has chosen the cash prize.</i>

344
00:27:44,560 --> 00:27:47,320
<i>All players who were shot,</i>
<i>please gather in the main hall.</i>

345
00:27:47,400 --> 00:27:48,720
Are you okay?

346
00:27:50,040 --> 00:27:51,280
I'm okay.

347
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,520
Are you two reliving old times?

348
00:27:54,840 --> 00:27:56,120
I thought you broke up.

349
00:27:57,080 --> 00:27:58,880
What do you care?

350
00:27:58,960 --> 00:28:00,680
And why are you here?

351
00:28:00,760 --> 00:28:03,040
Didn't you say you'd join
the national hockey team?

352
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:05,080
Guess you've hit rock bottom.

353
00:28:06,040 --> 00:28:07,240
Tangmo.

354
00:28:08,560 --> 00:28:10,200
You're not much better off than me.

355
00:28:11,640 --> 00:28:12,880
You'd better watch out.

356
00:28:14,080 --> 00:28:16,480
I'll pay you back tenfold in this game.

357
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:33,560
So what role did you get?

358
00:28:42,360 --> 00:28:43,760
I'm the bodyguard.

359
00:28:44,360 --> 00:28:45,520
What about you?

360
00:28:48,840 --> 00:28:50,160
Well,

361
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:53,240
what do you think?

362
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:55,360
A villager.

363
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,760
The important thing is to find out

364
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,440
who the wolves are.

365
00:29:14,120 --> 00:29:15,440
You guys were too busy fighting

366
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:16,880
and we all got shot.

367
00:29:53,640 --> 00:29:54,680
Hello?

368
00:29:55,280 --> 00:29:56,960
<i>So you finally picked up.</i>

369
00:29:57,040 --> 00:29:59,600
<i>I've been calling since morning.</i>
<i>It's almost evening!</i>

370
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:00,680
<i>How are you?</i>

371
00:30:01,360 --> 00:30:02,920
I didn't sleep well last night.

372
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:04,240
I still have a headache.

373
00:30:04,320 --> 00:30:05,800
<i>Have you taken your medicine?</i>

374
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:08,000
I have.

375
00:30:08,080 --> 00:30:10,880
<i>Just don't take more than</i>
<i>the doctor prescribed.</i>

376
00:30:13,040 --> 00:30:14,920
I know.

377
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:16,000
<i>Good.</i>

378
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:18,600
<i>About the link I sent you last night.</i>

379
00:30:18,680 --> 00:30:19,800
<i>the one about Pee.</i>

380
00:30:19,880 --> 00:30:22,680
<i>I think you need to push</i>
<i>harder to finish your novel.</i>

381
00:30:22,760 --> 00:30:24,120
<i>I'm begging you.</i>

382
00:30:24,200 --> 00:30:27,320
<i>I'm submitting the artwork</i>
<i>and proofs this week.</i>

383
00:30:27,400 --> 00:30:29,480
<i>We're falling too far behind him!</i>

384
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:33,320
Okay. Is that all?

385
00:31:37,760 --> 00:31:40,960
Search for the latest work
by the writer Pee.

386
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:48,680
LATEST WORK BY WRITER PEE

387
00:31:48,760 --> 00:31:51,240
<i>I WISH YOU WERE HERE</i>
BY PEE, THIWARAN CHINWARAWAT

388
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:56,800
For as long as I can remember,

389
00:31:56,880 --> 00:31:58,200
since I've known you,

390
00:31:59,600 --> 00:32:03,240
I've never seen you thinking
about a customer like this.

391
00:32:05,360 --> 00:32:06,720
That's not true.

392
00:32:06,800 --> 00:32:08,040
What customer?

393
00:32:10,440 --> 00:32:12,680
Do I really have to say which one?

394
00:32:13,680 --> 00:32:15,560
That writer, of course.

395
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:20,160
You said you wouldn't take his job,
but now you're always with him.

396
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:24,360
You know, you're so inseparable
that everyone here

397
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:26,160
has started betting

398
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:27,560
on whether you

399
00:32:27,640 --> 00:32:31,440
will end up with this customer.

400
00:32:31,520 --> 00:32:33,240
Did you secretly accept the job?

401
00:32:35,760 --> 00:32:37,440
I told you I didn't.

402
00:32:38,120 --> 00:32:39,640
He asked for research information,

403
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:41,680
so I gave it to him.

404
00:32:44,560 --> 00:32:46,040
You didn't take his job,

405
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:48,640
but he asked for research information,

406
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,760
and you gave it to him for free?

407
00:32:50,840 --> 00:32:53,280
Isn't that what you'd call
doing it willingly?

408
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,440
I just felt sorry for him.

409
00:32:55,520 --> 00:32:57,360
I help where I can.

410
00:32:57,440 --> 00:32:58,760
Do we really have to

411
00:32:58,840 --> 00:33:01,000
think about personal gain all the time?

412
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:09,000
You know, right?

413
00:33:10,360 --> 00:33:12,880
What pity can lead to?

414
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:22,200
Are you ready to get into this game?

415
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:06,000
Hello?

416
00:34:06,080 --> 00:34:07,080
How are you?

417
00:34:07,800 --> 00:34:09,239
<i>Where are you?</i>

418
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,560
<i>Why can I hear waves?</i>

419
00:34:11,639 --> 00:34:13,960
Why? Will you come see me if I tell you?

420
00:34:14,639 --> 00:34:15,639
Just tell me.

421
00:34:16,239 --> 00:34:17,360
Tell me first.

422
00:34:17,440 --> 00:34:18,920
You'll find out if I'm coming or not.

423
00:34:20,600 --> 00:34:21,800
I'm at the beach.

424
00:34:42,840 --> 00:34:44,000
Hey.

425
00:34:44,080 --> 00:34:45,280
Come take a shower with me.

426
00:34:45,360 --> 00:34:46,440
Are you crazy?

427
00:34:47,320 --> 00:34:48,440
What's with you?

428
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:51,000
Come on. I'll help you.

429
00:34:51,520 --> 00:34:52,760
Turn around.

430
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:55,159
Let go!

431
00:34:59,760 --> 00:35:01,840
Hey, be gentle! It might get caught!

432
00:35:06,200 --> 00:35:08,280
The zipper's so small.

433
00:35:09,720 --> 00:35:10,720
It won't catch anything.

434
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:12,240
You've got a smart mouth.

435
00:35:13,840 --> 00:35:14,840
I'm serious.

436
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:16,560
We need to shower together

437
00:35:17,760 --> 00:35:19,520
and watch each other's backs.

438
00:35:24,600 --> 00:35:25,920
Who do you think is a wolf?

439
00:35:27,120 --> 00:35:28,520
Definitely Cha.

440
00:35:28,600 --> 00:35:30,160
Look what he did to me today.

441
00:35:30,240 --> 00:35:31,520
Imagine what he'll do tonight.

442
00:35:33,680 --> 00:35:35,240
Do you have a grudge against him?

443
00:35:36,640 --> 00:35:40,560
You pulled strings to get on
the national team, so he didn't make it.

444
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:42,880
I made the national team on merit.

445
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:45,040
He wanted to win so badly

446
00:35:45,120 --> 00:35:46,720
because he doesn't
want anyone getting clues

447
00:35:46,800 --> 00:35:48,280
that he's the wolf.

448
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:51,560
But I think the others are suspicious too.

449
00:35:51,640 --> 00:35:52,560
Hey.

450
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:55,760
I think it's someone else

451
00:35:55,840 --> 00:35:57,000
who is a wolf.

452
00:35:59,080 --> 00:36:00,240
Who do you think it is?

453
00:36:01,960 --> 00:36:03,880
The guy named Au.

454
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:08,040
Did you have an ex with tattoos?

455
00:36:08,120 --> 00:36:09,480
Why are you so biased?

456
00:36:09,560 --> 00:36:11,040
If it's not him,

457
00:36:11,120 --> 00:36:13,280
another suspicious person

458
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:14,880
would be

459
00:36:16,720 --> 00:36:18,480
<i>the quiet one named Ploen.</i>

460
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:21,920
Why would an older woman like her

461
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,560
be in this game?

462
00:36:24,600 --> 00:36:25,920
There must be something going on.

463
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,080
But I think

464
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:28,440
<i>the guy named Nack</i>

465
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:30,560
<i>is suspicious too.</i>

466
00:36:31,200 --> 00:36:32,640
What about Wut?

467
00:36:33,360 --> 00:36:36,760
He doesn't seem very trustworthy either.

468
00:36:36,840 --> 00:36:38,880
But the most suspicious one

469
00:36:38,960 --> 00:36:39,800
is Ohm.

470
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:42,120
<i>He seems quiet and naive,</i>

471
00:36:42,200 --> 00:36:44,080
but when he shot at us,

472
00:36:45,480 --> 00:36:46,840
he didn't miss a single shot.

473
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:49,640
But anyway,

474
00:36:49,720 --> 00:36:50,640
I think

475
00:36:50,720 --> 00:36:52,920
we villagers should work together.

476
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:55,240
Because at least if we find the wolves

477
00:36:55,320 --> 00:36:57,280
and they're all dead,

478
00:36:57,360 --> 00:36:58,760
the rest of the game will be easy, right?

479
00:36:58,840 --> 00:37:00,480
How do you know

480
00:37:01,080 --> 00:37:02,760
we're not the wolves?

481
00:37:04,120 --> 00:37:05,720
My instincts are never wrong.

482
00:37:05,800 --> 00:37:06,800
Trust me.

483
00:37:10,360 --> 00:37:13,040
<i>It is now 5:30 p.m.</i>

484
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:17,040
<i>Everyone, please gather</i>
<i>in the Moon Room in half an hour.</i>

485
00:37:19,240 --> 00:37:21,760
<i>It is now 5:30 p.m.</i>

486
00:37:22,520 --> 00:37:26,200
<i>Everyone, please gather</i>
<i>in the Moon Room in half an hour.</i>

487
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:27,840
Hey, wait up!

488
00:37:51,280 --> 00:37:53,960
Welcome to the first night's wolf vote.

489
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:57,200
There are paper and pens in front of you.

490
00:37:57,760 --> 00:38:00,680
Write down who you think is a wolf.

491
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:02,720
Fold it and place it on your right.

492
00:38:02,800 --> 00:38:04,240
As for the bodyguard,

493
00:38:04,840 --> 00:38:07,680
write down who you want to
protect tonight.

494
00:38:09,360 --> 00:38:11,640
Can the bodyguard write their own name?

495
00:38:12,280 --> 00:38:13,680
Of course.

496
00:38:13,760 --> 00:38:15,280
That's selfish!

497
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:17,480
If the bodyguard writes
their own name every day,

498
00:38:17,560 --> 00:38:18,800
they'll survive until the end.

499
00:38:18,880 --> 00:38:20,360
The bodyguard's protection

500
00:38:21,240 --> 00:38:23,640
only protects against votes in this room.

501
00:38:23,720 --> 00:38:26,640
It doesn't guarantee survival
from the wolves' hunt.

502
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,560
If there are no more questions,

503
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:32,240
please cast your votes.

504
00:38:48,440 --> 00:38:49,520
Who are you voting for?

505
00:38:57,560 --> 00:39:00,120
Once you're done,
put your votes in the vase.

506
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:25,000
And now,

507
00:39:25,080 --> 00:39:27,680
the results of
the first night's wolf vote.

508
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:33,200
First,

509
00:39:35,520 --> 00:39:36,360
Ohm.

510
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:40,080
He got the first vote!

511
00:39:45,280 --> 00:39:46,160
Tangmo.

512
00:39:47,320 --> 00:39:48,640
Congratulations.

513
00:39:54,960 --> 00:39:56,320
Cha.

514
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:03,480
Wut.

515
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,480
And the final vote

516
00:40:10,080 --> 00:40:11,560
tonight…

517
00:40:16,200 --> 00:40:17,040
goes to Ohm.

518
00:40:19,160 --> 00:40:20,680
Congratulations.

519
00:40:23,120 --> 00:40:25,600
But we still have
the bodyguard's protection.

520
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:27,160
And tonight,

521
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:30,400
the bodyguard has chosen to protect…

522
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:37,840
Wut.

523
00:40:40,400 --> 00:40:44,640
That means the player
voted to be burned tonight

524
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:46,960
is Ohm,

525
00:40:47,760 --> 00:40:48,880
who is a villager.

526
00:40:50,080 --> 00:40:51,240
Burned?

527
00:40:51,320 --> 00:40:52,960
You don't mean literally, right?

528
00:40:53,040 --> 00:40:54,200
Of course not.

529
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:57,960
It's just a metaphor
for eliminating a player.

530
00:40:59,600 --> 00:41:02,520
We choose to eliminate players
in a civilized manner.

531
00:41:09,320 --> 00:41:10,320
You idiots!

532
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:14,120
I'm a villager!

533
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:18,560
You've lost an innocent person!

534
00:41:19,160 --> 00:41:20,200
Happy now?

535
00:41:22,200 --> 00:41:23,760
But fuck it.

536
00:41:25,120 --> 00:41:27,120
At least I won the mini-game

537
00:41:27,880 --> 00:41:29,880
and got 100,000 baht.

538
00:41:43,840 --> 00:41:45,120
Hey! What the fuck?

539
00:41:45,200 --> 00:41:46,920
What the hell?
What the fuck are you doing?

540
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:48,360
Calm down.

541
00:41:49,360 --> 00:41:50,640
Calm down.

542
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:52,520
- Hey, don't push!
- Everyone, please sit down.

543
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:54,440
Like hell we'll sit down!
What are you doing?

544
00:41:54,520 --> 00:41:56,040
- Sit down. He told us to.
- Yeah, sit down.

545
00:41:56,120 --> 00:41:57,760
- Go on, sit down.
- Sit down!

546
00:42:01,680 --> 00:42:03,160
As you all know,

547
00:42:03,960 --> 00:42:06,240
everyone has signed a contract

548
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:08,800
agreeing to the rules of this game.

549
00:42:10,880 --> 00:42:12,640
No one is allowed to withdraw

550
00:42:13,840 --> 00:42:15,360
until the game ends.

551
00:42:15,440 --> 00:42:17,120
And from now on,

552
00:42:17,960 --> 00:42:20,560
once you all leave this room,

553
00:42:22,560 --> 00:42:24,480
the wolves' hunt will begin.

554
00:42:27,080 --> 00:42:29,600
All villagers may use any area

555
00:42:29,680 --> 00:42:31,080
of this mansion

556
00:42:32,280 --> 00:42:33,840
to escape,

557
00:42:33,920 --> 00:42:34,840
hide,

558
00:42:35,600 --> 00:42:38,040
or defend themselves against the wolves.

559
00:42:40,760 --> 00:42:43,400
When the music plays in the morning,

560
00:42:44,920 --> 00:42:46,840
the hunt will be over.

561
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:50,640
You will all get to rest.

562
00:42:53,720 --> 00:42:55,240
Please get ready.

563
00:43:03,880 --> 00:43:05,760
What the fuck kind of game is this?

564
00:43:17,280 --> 00:43:18,360
Yoyeh!

565
00:43:18,440 --> 00:43:19,560
Let's hurry!

566
00:43:39,800 --> 00:43:41,160
Let me go!

567
00:43:41,240 --> 00:43:42,200
Let me go!

568
00:43:42,280 --> 00:43:44,800
Let me go, damn it! I want to go home!

569
00:43:44,880 --> 00:43:46,680
I'm not playing anymore!

570
00:43:46,760 --> 00:43:47,680
Let me go!

571
00:43:47,760 --> 00:43:51,120
Let me go! I want to see my child!

572
00:43:51,200 --> 00:43:54,040
Let me go!

573
00:43:56,080 --> 00:43:57,760
Don't shoot me!

574
00:44:04,040 --> 00:44:04,880
‪Hey!

575
00:44:05,400 --> 00:44:06,240
‪Hey!

576
00:44:07,360 --> 00:44:08,960
<i>Let me repeat the rules.</i>

577
00:44:09,040 --> 00:44:11,800
<i>Only one winner will leave this place.</i>

578
00:44:11,880 --> 00:44:14,440
<i>If any player tries to break the rules</i>

579
00:44:14,520 --> 00:44:16,080
<i>by leaving the premises,</i>

580
00:44:16,160 --> 00:44:18,760
<i>that player will face</i>
<i>the ultimate punishment</i>

581
00:44:18,840 --> 00:44:20,640
<i>from our rabbit staff.</i>

582
00:44:20,720 --> 00:44:23,720
<i>As I said, you can leave this place</i>

583
00:44:23,800 --> 00:44:25,440
<i>in only one way.</i>

584
00:44:25,520 --> 00:44:26,640
<i>By winning this game.</i>

585
00:44:27,200 --> 00:44:28,960
- Hey!
- Don't!

586
00:44:29,040 --> 00:44:30,320
Don't go!

587
00:44:30,400 --> 00:44:31,840
- Help me first!
- Come on, Yoyeh!

588
00:44:31,920 --> 00:44:33,120
- Tangmo!
- Go!

589
00:44:33,200 --> 00:44:34,240
Help me!

590
00:45:06,440 --> 00:45:07,400
Hey.

591
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:14,920
Hey.

592
00:46:05,440 --> 00:46:06,400
Hey.

593
00:46:07,760 --> 00:46:08,760
Hey.

594
00:46:11,560 --> 00:46:12,520
Hey.

595
00:46:13,640 --> 00:46:15,520
Is this really the time
to play in the water?

596
00:46:25,760 --> 00:46:26,760
Hey.

597
00:46:28,280 --> 00:46:29,280
Hey.

598
00:46:36,560 --> 00:46:37,520
Hey.

599
00:46:45,680 --> 00:46:47,200
Hey! Hey!

600
00:46:48,520 --> 00:46:49,560
Hey.

601
00:47:42,440 --> 00:47:43,800
It's because of him, isn't it?

602
00:47:45,440 --> 00:47:46,560
The one named Pee.

603
00:47:52,760 --> 00:47:54,440
I happened to overhear that day.

604
00:48:11,400 --> 00:48:12,800
I have nothing left.

605
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:19,600
My career.

606
00:48:25,520 --> 00:48:27,400
I used to have Pee by my side.

607
00:48:36,320 --> 00:48:38,240
I can't live without him.

608
00:48:42,360 --> 00:48:44,000
But you still have me.

609
00:50:43,240 --> 00:50:44,920
Come in! Come in!

610
00:51:02,480 --> 00:51:04,840
What kind of crazy game
have you brought me into?

611
00:51:04,920 --> 00:51:06,880
How the hell was I supposed to know

612
00:51:06,960 --> 00:51:08,440
it would turn out like this?

613
00:51:08,520 --> 00:51:10,440
If we get out of here,

614
00:51:10,520 --> 00:51:12,240
I'll have to get your brain checked.

615
00:51:12,320 --> 00:51:13,800
You saw what happened.

616
00:51:13,880 --> 00:51:16,400
Ohm got shot. Blood went everywhere.

617
00:51:16,480 --> 00:51:17,960
And then there's Ploen.

618
00:51:21,120 --> 00:51:24,200
I wouldn't be surprised
if a wolf ripped your throat out.

619
00:51:25,040 --> 00:51:26,040
Really?

620
00:51:27,120 --> 00:51:28,200
But…

621
00:51:29,120 --> 00:51:31,240
This isn't the time to think!

622
00:51:31,320 --> 00:51:32,960
We need to find somewhere to hide.

623
00:51:38,200 --> 00:51:39,560
Help!

624
00:51:39,640 --> 00:51:41,080
Help! Somebody help me!

625
00:51:41,160 --> 00:51:42,400
I'm begging you!

626
00:51:42,480 --> 00:51:43,440
Let me go!

627
00:51:43,520 --> 00:51:45,480
- Don't, Yoyeh!
- I'm scared!

628
00:51:46,280 --> 00:51:47,280
You saw her.

629
00:51:47,360 --> 00:51:49,160
She was just running from the wolves.

630
00:51:49,240 --> 00:51:50,520
She was about to get out.

631
00:51:50,600 --> 00:51:52,520
Have you forgotten about the wolves?

632
00:51:53,960 --> 00:51:56,000
- It's coming!
- Don't!

633
00:51:56,080 --> 00:51:57,040
It's coming!

634
00:51:57,120 --> 00:51:58,480
- If you won't help, I will!
- Don't!

635
00:51:58,560 --> 00:52:00,480
It's coming!

636
00:52:00,560 --> 00:52:02,520
Hurry! Hurry!

637
00:52:46,800 --> 00:52:49,680
I told you not to trust
anyone in this game.

638
00:52:58,320 --> 00:53:00,520
Don't follow me!

639
00:53:00,600 --> 00:53:01,840
I'm scared!

640
00:53:01,920 --> 00:53:03,080
- Please let me go!
- Yoyeh!

641
00:53:03,600 --> 00:53:04,880
Yoyeh!

642
00:53:05,480 --> 00:53:07,080
We need to find somewhere to hide.

643
00:53:07,160 --> 00:53:08,440
Go!

644
00:53:53,000 --> 00:53:56,400
<i>We have a werewolf kill.</i>
<i>Villager Ploen has been eliminated.</i>

645
00:55:33,920 --> 00:55:35,880
I'll take your job.

646
00:55:37,840 --> 00:55:38,840
What did you say?

647
00:55:38,920 --> 00:55:41,400
<i>If you want me to be</i>
<i>the model for your novel,</i>

648
00:55:41,480 --> 00:55:42,360
<i>I'll take the job.</i>

649
00:55:42,440 --> 00:55:43,960
At 3 p.m. today,

650
00:55:44,040 --> 00:55:45,880
we'll play Capture the Flag.

651
00:55:45,960 --> 00:55:49,560
<i>If any player</i>
<i>loses their flag to the opposing team,</i>

652
00:55:49,640 --> 00:55:50,520
<i>they'll be eliminated immediately.</i>

653
00:55:52,520 --> 00:55:53,480
Shit!

654
00:55:53,560 --> 00:55:55,680
If you make me lose again,

655
00:55:55,760 --> 00:55:57,920
you'd better watch out.

656
00:55:58,520 --> 00:56:01,120
<i>Tonight, two players have</i>
<i>received the same number of votes.</i>
